{
  "path": "lua/ge/extensions/editor/toolUtilities/render/lines.lua",
  "module": "Debug line drawing for the editor's spline editing tools (from the old monolithic render.lua). Each function draws a segment p0-p1 with the style (color, thickness) matching a use: spline, wireframe, elevation drop line, normal, navigation, etc. Leaf module: depends on utils/debugDraw, the shared style and util (blue-to-red color ramp).",
  "usage": "local rLines = require('editor/toolUtilities/render/lines')\nrLines.drawSplineLine(vec3(0,0,10), vec3(5,0,10))",
  "notes": [
    "The \"culled\" variants only draw if BOTH endpoints are within 600 m of the camera; drawSplineLine, drawArcSegment, drawJoinLine and drawLineImmediate are not filtered.",
    "Colors are packed integers (color() function) coming from editor/toolUtilities/style.",
    "drawWireFrameLine modifies p0.z and p1.z by +0.05 (side effect on the arguments) while its copies offsetP0/offsetP1 are drawn without the offset: the intended offset is not applied to the drawing."
  ],
  "functions": {
    "drawLineImmediate": {
      "desc": "Draws a line without distance filtering (debugDraw.drawLineInstance_MinArg).",
      "params": {
        "p0": {
          "type": "vec3",
          "desc": "Start."
        },
        "p1": {
          "type": "vec3",
          "desc": "End."
        },
        "thickness": {
          "type": "number",
          "desc": "Thickness."
        },
        "col": {
          "type": "integer",
          "desc": "Packed color."
        }
      },
      "returns": []
    },
    "drawLineCulled": {
